==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
Probably related to {{m|ru|тук||fat, lard}}, {{m|ru|тыть||[[тучнеть]], to grow stout/fat, to put on flesh}} as {{noncog|ru|кры́ша||roof}} related to {{noncog|ru|крыть||to cover, to roof}} (Vasmer, Shansky, Tsyganenko). Alternatively related to {{m|ru|ту́хнуть}} (mentioned by Vasmer); or to {{m|ru|то́щий}}, or from Turkic (Chernych).

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|ту́ша}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|ту́ша|dim=ту́шка}}

# [[carcass]]
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|derogatory}} fat person
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|derogatory}} [[meathead]], stupid muscular person

